nly 7  percent of metro's police force  and 10 percent of the entire staff  including civilians  officer hunt says that's a cause for  concern my thing is to always push and  push  into you know to get more people who  look like me  to join the department metro has a  multicultural advisory council that  provides  feedback to the sheriff monthly however  coward holmen says black  officers should be at the table with  leadership more often and help train the  department when it comes to racial  issues  she says frequent cultural awareness  classes can save lives  who better to teach these classes than  the people who work for you  who actually know both sides of the  story coward holmen says tension  embedded in our country's history  can only be healed by working together  we've been  in this community pounding the sand for  20 years but for the last eight years  we've been pounding it hard because we  have to make a change  and the department can't do it by  themselves reporting bianca holman  8 news now tomorrow night the i-team's  vanessa murphy will be looking at use of  force policies and also how complaints  against metro police officers  are investigated those reports are  coming up at 5 and 11 o'clock  and we also have more information on  police use of force  hirings and firings and diversity on the  force on 8newsnow.com  just be sure to click on the banner on  the front page that says the state of  metro  metro police
 

